legend:
C++ has several basic data types. The most common ones are:
\begin{itemize}
\item \texttt{int} — a 32-bit integer;
\item \texttt{long long} — a 64-bit integer;
\item \texttt{char} — a single character;
\item \texttt{float} — a 32-bit real number;
\item \texttt{double} — a 64-bit real number.
\end{itemize}
A variable is read with \texttt{cin >> name;} and printed with \texttt{cout << name;}. Read one value of each type and print them back.
